dataset.py: Contains the dataset classes used in the whole project

match_clips.py: Matches frames in FRAME_DIRS with video (clips) in CLIP_DIRS; saved into matching_results_{}.json.
We need this later to create a consistent dataset split for both the frame-based and video-based models

match_grades.py: Use matching_results_{}.json and the official grading in DR_Grading_Summary_v3.csv to extract the grading;
saved into clip_labels_{}.json and image_labels_{}.json

split_data.py: Create stratified split (original 5 grades) video-based with clip_labels_{}.json and get the frame-based split
using matching_results_{}.json. The split is 0.8 to 0.2 video-wise and only approximately 0.8 to 0.2 frame-wise.

